      <title>The Miraculous Plant Being Eaten To Extinction 2000 Years Ago, Is Still Around</title>
      <link>https://thenewsbeans.com/the-miraculous-plant-being-eaten-to-extinction-2000-years-ago-is-still-around/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=the-miraculous-plant-being-eaten-to-extinction-2000-years-ago-is-still-around</link>
      <description>According to a report by national geographic, the golden-flowered shrub known as silphion was one of the most sought-after goods in the Mediterranean region from before Athens's foundation until the Roman Empire's height. Ancient Greek doctors revered Silphion as a universal remedy from stomach aches to wart eradication.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://thenewsbeans.com/the-miraculous-plant-being-eaten-to-extinction-2000-years-ago-is-still-around/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=the-miraculous-plant-being-eaten-to-extinction-2000-years-ago-is-still-around</guid>
